 "description": "The one address grammar (router/classify.py parse_address). Each case: `in`, and either `out` (the canonical form: the domain lowercased, the local part exactly as given) or `malformed: true`. Shared with the external leg's runtime so the two parsers cannot drift. The fleet-name rule (a local part at a fleet domain must also match the registry name grammar) is context-dependent and is not in these vectors.",
